  "ref": "DEU.17.8",
  "review_notes": [
    "Three בֵּין … לְ pairs, each with its own written *between*: every pair-opening בֵּין takes one and each לְ takes the *and* standing where the connective stands (rule 26); the single waw at s017 takes the *and* before the third pair.",
    "The presentative recasting at s002 is the verse's one materially contested unit: *there arise ... too hard* is one verb's rendering, headed on *hard* rather than *arise*.",
    "s039–s040 (בּוֹ) are unrendered by the ASV in this verse."
  ]
